   {"issue": "Section 2.01(a) provides that none of the Securities Administrator, Master Servicer nor Indenture Trustee \"shall be obligated or permitted to fund any such Draws\", yet this paragraph has the Securities Administrator agreeing to \"direct funds\" to reimburse Servicer Draw advances. The two paragraphs pull against each other on the Securities Administrator's role in Draw funding.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The paragraph says only that it \"is not intended\" that any HELOC be a high-cost loan while adding that \"the Depositor so represents and recognizes\", so whether this is a binding representation or a mere statement of intent is genuinely uncertain. Clause (v) compounds this by referring to the \"then current\" S&P LEVELS Glossary \"which is now Version 5.7 Revised\", leaving the operative version indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.35},
