   {"issue": "The deferral of repurchase or substitution until an Opinion of Counsel is obtained can push a substitution past the absolute two-year cut-off imposed by the last sentence of Section 2.04. Which provision prevails when the opinion arrives late is not addressed.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c022", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Indenture Trustee and Owner Trustee \"shall require the Sponsor, at its option, to either\" substitute or repurchase — the antecedent of \"its\" is ambiguous as between the Sponsor and the requiring trustees. Who chooses between substitution and repurchase is therefore unsettled.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c023", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.06},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.05}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c024", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.08},
   {"issue": "This representation asserts \"full corporate power\" although Section 2.06(i) represents the Depositor to be a Delaware limited liability company, and Section 2.06(iii) likewise refers to \"corporate action\" and \"certificate of formation or by-laws\". The entity form described in the same series of representations is internally inconsistent.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c025", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.06},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c026", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.05},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.05}
